Finding: {"title":"DELETE /locations/:id and PUT /locations/:id only require requireAuth() — any org role (student, instructor) can deactivate or rename the school's location","severity":"HIGH","area":"Authorization / privilege escalation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-locations.ts"],"detail":"Lines 2792 (PUT) and 2839 (DELETE) declare requireAuth() with no {roles: [...]} restriction. requireAuth() (src/server/middleware/auth.ts:153) accepts any authenticated role when options.roles is omitted. The DELETE handler does soft-delete (sets status to 'inactive' per the comment at line 2838) and does correctly check flightSchoolId !== orgId for tenant scoping, but performs no role check — so a low-privileged member of the correct org (e.g. a student account) can deactivate the entire flight school location or edit its name/address/contact info.","impact":"A compromised or malicious low-privilege account (student/instructor) within a legitimate org can take the school's location offline (soft-delete) or corrupt its contact/address data, a business-critical operation that should be admin-gated.","recommendation":"Change both routes to requireAuth({ roles: ['admin', 'super_admin'] }) or requireAdmin(), consistent with the 14 other routes in this file that already use requireAdmin() for comparable destructive/administrative operations.","confidence":"high"}
